## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design scalable, multi-tenant data architectures that respect data residency requirements while optimizing for cost and performance across distributed regions.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-aware routing and data residency enforcement
- Per-tenant idempotency patterns and deduplication strategies
- Cross-region cost optimization and traffic management
- Schema evolution compatibility in distributed systems
- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry tracing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tenant routing resolution
function getRegionForTenant(tenantId) {
  const tenantConfig = dynamodb.get(tenantId);
  return tenantConfig.region || getDefaultRegion();
}

function routeEvent(event) {
  const region = getRegionForTenant(event.tenantId);
  const stream = getKinesisStream(region);
  return stream.putRecord({
    partitionKey: `${event.tenantId}_${event.timestamp}`,
    data: JSON.stringify(event),
    dedupeId: generateDedupeId(event)
  });
}
```

## Critical Success Factors
- Automatic region selection based on tenant profile
- Strong consistency in routing decisions
- Graceful handling of schema evolution across regions
- Comprehensive observability of cross-region operations

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time masking, per-tenant isolation, cross-region data flow, and how governance (KMS keys, Glue catalog, Athena access) interacts with retention and backfill.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time data masking with per-tenant keys
- Cross-region ingest and separate raw/audit data streams
- Tenant-scoped S3 prefixes and Athena access control
- Schema evolution and retention policies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda mask skeleton (pseudo)
exports.handler = async (e) => {
  const tenant = e.tenantId;
  const masked = maskFields(e, tenant); // uses per-tenant KMS key
  await storeMasked(masked, tenant);
  await storeRaw(e, tenant);
};
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test masking correctness across tenants at scale?
- How would you handle a tenant key rotation without downtime?
